# Production build — loaded automatically by `vite build` (Vercel runs this).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing is hardcoded here on purpose. `.env.production` outranks `.env.local`,
# so a value committed here would silently override the local build — which
# breaks the native iOS build on the Mac (it has no Vercel dashboard to read).
#
# Set these in the Vercel dashboard (museum-app → Settings → Environment
# Variables) for the web build — real env vars outrank every .env file:
#   VITE_API_URL              backend origin (the EC2 server)
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#   VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
#
# For the native iOS build, put the same values in `.env.local` on the Mac
# before `npm run build && npx cap sync` — plus VITE_APPLE_PAY_MERCHANT_ID.
